{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019SDbDXFAAR5R9ceauxhNvw","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel04.0-uc001-ls\n     2→title: \"List directory contents via ls (core flags)\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go ls binary on a known fixture directory with core flags (default,\n     6→  -1, -l, -a, -A, -d, --color, -h). The differential testing harness runs both the Go binary\n     7→  and the Homebrew reference binary (gls from coreutils) with the same arguments and\n     8→  environment, applies an LsNormalizer to both outputs (replacing mtime columns with a fixed\n     9→  placeholder), and confirms that the normalized outputs are identical. All tests run with\n    10→  --color=never and LC_ALL=C to eliminate ANSI and locale variance.\n    11→\n    12→actor: Human Operator\n    13→\n    14→trigger: |\n    15→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd008-ls.yaml) and shared component PRDs\n    16→  (pkg/sys, pkg/format from rel00.0) and invokes do-work to produce a passing differential\n    17→  test for cmd/ls core flags.\n    18→\n    19→flow:\n    20→  - id: F1\n    21→    step: |\n    22→      The operator runs the Go ls binary on a fixture directory with known file types,\n    23→      sizes, and permissions. Example: ./bin/ls --color=never testdata/ls-fixture/\n    24→  - id: F2\n    25→    step: |\n    26→      cmd/ls reads the directory entries, queries terminal width via pkg/sys.TerminalWidth\n    27→      (for default multi-column mode), and obtains file metadata via pkg/sys.Stat for long\n    28→      format. It formats output via pkg/format.Columns (multi-column) or inline formatting\n    29→      (long format with pkg/format.HumanSize for -h).\n    30→  - id: F3\n    31→    step: |\n    32→      cmd/ls writes the formatted listing to stdout. The format depends on the active flags:\n    33→      multi-column (default TTY), single-column (default pipe or -1), or long format (-l).\n    34→  - id: F4\n    35→    step: |\n    36→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/ls and gls with\n    37→      the same arguments, environment (LC_ALL=C, --color=never), and working directory.\n    38→  - id: F5\n    39→    step: |\n    40→      The harness applies the LsNormalizer to both outputs. The LsNormalizer replaces the\n    41→      modification time column in -l output (fields matching \"Mon DD HH:MM\" or \"Mon DD  YYYY\")\n    42→      with the placeholder \"MTIME\". This eliminates wall-clock divergence between runs.\n    43→  - id: F6\n    44→    step: |\n    45→      The harness compares the normalized outputs byte-for-byte. Both binaries must produce\n    46→      identical entry names, sort order, column layout, and field values (permissions,\n    47→      hard-link count, owner, group, size).\n    48→  - id: F7\n    49→    step: |\n    50→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    51→      triggering args, both raw outputs, both normalized outputs, and both exit codes.\n    52→\n    53→touchpoints:\n    54→  - T1: \"cmd/ls — directory listing, format modes, filter flags, color, human sizes (prd008-ls R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6, R7)\"\n    55→  - T2: \"pkg/sys — TerminalWidth, Stat/Lstat, IsTerminal, InstallSIGPIPEHandler, OnTerminalResize (rel00.0 infrastructure)\"\n    56→  - T3: \"pkg/format — Columns, FileTypeColor, HumanSize (rel00.0 infrastructure)\"\n    57→  - T4: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, LsNormalizer, binary execution and comparison\"\n    58→\n    59→success_criteria:\n    60→  - id: S1\n    61→    criterion: cmd/ls compiles and ./bin/ls exists after mage build.\n    62→  - id: S2\n    63→    criterion: |\n    64→      Default mode with stdout redirected (not a TTY) produces single-column output with\n    65→      one entry per line, matching gls output on the same fixture.\n    66→  - id: S3\n    67→    criterion: |\n    68→      -l long format produces identical output to gls -l after MTIME normalization on the\n    69→      same fixture directory.\n    70→  - id: S4\n    71→    criterion: |\n    72→      -a includes dotfiles (including . and ..) and matches gls -a output on a fixture\n    73→      containing dotfiles.\n    74→  - id: S5\n    75→    criterion: |\n    76→      --color=never produces output with no ANSI escape sequences, matching gls --color=never\n    77→      byte-for-byte.\n    78→  - id: S6\n    79→    criterion: |\n    80→      -lh produces human-readable file sizes that match gls -lh on files with known sizes.\n    81→  - id: S7\n    82→    criterion: |\n    83→      The differential test passes for all core flags: default (single-col redirect),\n    84→      -1, -l, -lh, -a, -A, -d, --color=never. All tests use LC_ALL=C and --color=never\n    85→      (except color-specific tests).\n    86→\n    87→out_of_scope:\n    88→  - Default multi-column mode on a real TTY is difficult to test deterministically in the\n    89→    harness; we test -C explicitly in the ls extended use case (rel04.1).\n    90→  - Owner/group name normalization is not applied; tests use a fixture where files are owned\n    91→    by the test runner's UID/GID, ensuring consistency.\n    92→  - SIGWINCH behavior is specified in prd008-ls R7.2 but is not directly testable in the\n    93→    differential harness.\n    94→\n    95→test_suite: test-rel04.0\n    96→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ec5f9a0-75f0-4bb6-b3e8-4454c4b170d0","uuid":"b3c0a6f4-5ec5-495e-beaa-3fe1dac6c9f3","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/308/docs/specs/use-cases/rel04.0-uc001-ls.yaml","content":"id: rel04.0-uc001-ls\ntitle: \"List directory contents via ls (core flags)\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go ls binary on a known fixture directory with core flags (default,\n  -1, -l, -a, -A, -d, --color, -h). The differential testing harness runs both the Go binary\n  and the Homebrew reference binary (gls from coreutils) with the same arguments and\n  environment, applies an LsNormalizer to both outputs (replacing mtime columns with a fixed\n  placeholder), and confirms that the normalized outputs are identical. All tests run with\n  --color=never and LC_ALL=C to eliminate ANSI and locale variance.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd008-ls.yaml) and shared component PRDs\n  (pkg/sys, pkg/format from rel00.0) and invokes do-work to produce a passing differential\n  test for cmd/ls core flags.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go ls binary on a fixture directory with known file types,\n      sizes, and permissions. Example: ./bin/ls --color=never testdata/ls-fixture/\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/ls reads the directory entries, queries terminal width via pkg/sys.TerminalWidth\n      (for default multi-column mode), and obtains file metadata via pkg/sys.Stat for long\n      format. It formats output via pkg/format.Columns (multi-column) or inline formatting\n      (long format with pkg/format.HumanSize for -h).\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      cmd/ls writes the formatted listing to stdout. The format depends on the active flags:\n      multi-column (default TTY), single-column (default pipe or -1), or long format (-l).\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/ls and gls with\n      the same arguments, environment (LC_ALL=C, --color=never), and working directory.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness applies the LsNormalizer to both outputs. The LsNormalizer replaces the\n      modification time column in -l output (fields matching \"Mon DD HH:MM\" or \"Mon DD  YYYY\")\n      with the placeholder \"MTIME\". This eliminates wall-clock divergence between runs.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The harness compares the normalized outputs byte-for-byte. Both binaries must produce\n      identical entry names, sort order, column layout, and field values (permissions,\n      hard-link count, owner, group, size).\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both raw outputs, both normalized outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/ls — directory listing, format modes, filter flags, color, human sizes (prd008-ls R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6, R7)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/sys — TerminalWidth, Stat/Lstat, IsTerminal, InstallSIGPIPEHandler, OnTerminalResize (rel00.0 infrastructure)\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/format — Columns, FileTypeColor, HumanSize (rel00.0 infrastructure)\"\n  - T4: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, LsNormalizer, binary execution and comparison\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/ls compiles and ./bin/ls exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: |\n      Default mode with stdout redirected (not a TTY) produces single-column output with\n      one entry per line, matching gls output on the same fixture.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: |\n      -l long format produces identical output to gls -l after MTIME normalization on the\n      same fixture directory.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: |\n      -a includes dotfiles (including . and ..) and matches gls -a output on a fixture\n      containing dotfiles.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: |\n      --color=never produces output with no ANSI escape sequences, matching gls --color=never\n      byte-for-byte.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: |\n      -lh produces human-readable file sizes that match gls -lh on files with known sizes.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test passes for all core flags: default (single-col redirect),\n      -1, -l, -lh, -a, -A, -d, --color=never. All tests use LC_ALL=C and --color=never\n      (except color-specific tests).\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Default multi-column mode on a real TTY is difficult to test deterministically in the\n    harness; we test -C explicitly in the ls extended use case (rel04.1).\n  - Owner/group name normalization is not applied; tests use a fixture where files are owned\n    by the test runner's UID/GID, ensuring consistency.\n  - SIGWINCH behavior is specified in prd008-ls R7.2 but is not directly testable in the\n    differential harness.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel04.0\n","numLines":96,"startLine":1,"totalLines":96}}}
