{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QWAxX9bSpui43uDNwG4Nwy","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel04.0\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel04.0 — ls core flag listing\"\n     3→release: rel04.0\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel04.0-uc001-ls\n     7→  - prd008-ls R1\n     8→  - prd008-ls R2\n     9→  - prd008-ls R3\n    10→  - prd008-ls R4\n    11→  - prd008-ls R5\n    12→  - prd008-ls R6\n    13→  - prd008-ls R7\n    14→\n    15→preconditions:\n    16→  - Binaries exist under ./bin/ (built via mage build).\n    17→  - Reference binaries are installed via Homebrew gls (coreutils).\n    18→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/ls/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    19→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    20→  - All differential tests use --color=never to eliminate ANSI escape variance (except color-specific structural tests).\n    21→  - For -l tests, the LsNormalizer replaces the mtime column with the placeholder MTIME before comparison.\n    22→  - Tests use a fixture directory (testdata/ls-fixture/) containing regular files of known sizes, a subdirectory, dotfiles, a symbolic link, and files with known permissions.\n    23→\n    24→test_cases:\n    25→  - name: ls_default_single_col_redirect\n    26→    description: 'No flags, stdout redirected (not a TTY); one entry per line in C locale order. stdout is a pipe (not TTY), so default format is single-column'\n    27→    inputs:\n    28→      args: [\"--color=never\", \"testdata/ls-fixture/\"]\n    29→      stdin: null\n    30→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    31→    normalization: none\n    32→    expected:\n    33→      exit_code: 0\n    34→      stdout_structure: one entry per line, sorted in C locale order, no dotfiles\n    35→      stderr: \"\"\n    36→    traces:\n    37→      - prd008-ls R1.2\n    38→      - prd008-ls R1.3\n    39→      - prd008-ls R1.4\n    40→\n    41→  - name: ls_default_multi_col_tty\