noticing a potential issue with the filter logic where I'm using `strings.HasPrefix` to detect hidden files. Let me trace through the default filter case to make sure it's correctly skipping dotfiles.\n\nFor the default filter, I skip entries starting with \".\" since we only add \".\" and \"..\" when using filterAll. The filterAlmostAll case works correctly too—it shows dotfiles but excludes \".\" and \"..\" since ReadDir doesn't return those anyway.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the `needNewline` logic for when file operands are mixed with directories. The pattern should be: print files, then for each directory add a blank line before the header, print the header and entries. Let me verify this flows correctly through the output logic.\n\nWhen there are only directories with no files, the first directory shouldn't have a blank line before it, but subsequent ones should. And if there's just a single directory with no files, it shouldn't print a header at all—just the entries. For edge cases like `ls nonexistent dir1`, the nonexistent file fails and we exit with an error.\n\nActually, I'm realizing that when we have both an error and a directory listing, they go to separate streams so the blank line behavior depends on buffering. My approach of keeping them separate is the right call. I'm ready to implement this now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9359,"cache_read_input_tokens":90571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9359,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ec5f9a0-75f0-4bb6-b3e8-4454c4b170d0","uuid":"dbfca3a8-56fb-4f2f-b4c9-963ac1db8cca"}
